<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- gorpEndpoint: default -->
<gorp>
  <expect>Unit handling, one case per algorithm. Measured on GORP 3561df2, 2026-09-14: cases 1-26 and 28 answer as listed; 27 is wrong; 29-32 are HTTP 500. The editor declares each result unit on &lt;Math&gt;. 1. AddSameUnit: 8 m. 2. AddKilometerAndMeter: 2.5 km. 3. AddHourAndMinute: 1.5 h. 4. AddLiterAndMilliliter: 1.25 L. 5. SubtractGramFromKilogram: 1.5 kg. 6. AddLiteralToMeasured: 5 m (the 2 takes x's unit). 7. NegateMeasured: -7 m. 8. GlucoseAdd: 120 mg/dL. 9. AreaMeterTimesMeter: 15 m². 10. VolumeThreeLengths: 24 m³. 11. EnergyNewtonTimesMeter: 15 J. 12. PowerJoulePerSecond: 25 W. 13. SpeedMeterPerSecond: 2.5 m/s. 14. SpeedKilometerPerHour: 45 km/h. 15. AccelerationSpeedOverTime: 5 m/s². 16. ForceMassTimesAcceleration: 19.6 N. 17. PressureForceOverArea: 25 Pa. 18. OhmsLawVoltsOverAmps: 4 Ω. 19. FrequencyOneOverPeriod: 2 Hz. 20. ReciprocalLength: 0.5 1/m. 21. RatioSameUnit: 0.5 (a plain fraction). 22. RatioMixedUnits: 4 (a plain fraction; km and m convert). 23. ScaleByLiteral: 6 m. 24. ScaleByPlainVariable: 6 m. 25. SquareByLiteralExponent: 9 m². 26. CubeByLiteralExponent: 27 m³. 27. TemperatureAddCelsius: WRONG TODAY: GORP answers 298.15 °C (both added as absolute kelvin, 293.15 + 278.15, shown back in °C). Expected 25 °C, reading the second value as a difference, as Celsius+Kelvin already does. 28. TemperatureCelsiusPlusKelvin: 25 °C (GORP reads the 5 K as a difference). Compare with TemperatureAddCelsius, which does not. 29. SquareRootOfArea: 4 m. FAILS TODAY (HTTP 500) even with the result unit declared: a fractional power of a measured value. 30. PowerByVariableExponent: EXPECTED TO FAIL (HTTP 500): the result unit depends on y's value, so nothing can declare it. 31. AddPlainVariable: SHOULD REFUSE: meters plus a plain variable. Today a bare HTTP 500, ideally a message. 32. AddMismatchedUnits: MUST REFUSE: meters plus seconds. The editor flags it; GORP should answer with a message, not a bare 500.</expect>
  <algorithms>
    <algorithm namespace="UnitTests.Units.AddSameUnit">
      <function>
        <expressions>
          <expression sequence="0">
            <Math>
              <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
                <apply><plus/><ci>x</ci><ci>y</ci></apply>
              </math>
            </Math>
          </expression>
        </expressions>
      </function>
      <inputs>
        <x unit="\metre">3</x>
        <y unit="\metre">5</y>
      </inputs>
    </algorithm>
    <algorithm namespace="UnitTests.Units.AddKilometerAndMeter">
      <function>
        <expressions>
          <expression sequence="0">
            <Math>
              <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
                <apply><plus/><ci>x</ci><ci>y</ci></apply>
              </math>
            </Math>
          </expression>
        </expressions>
      </function>
      <inputs>
        <x unit="\kilo\metre">2</x>
        <y unit="\metre">500</y>
      </inputs>
    </algorithm>
    <algorithm namespace="UnitTests.Units.AddHourAndMinute">
      <function>
        <expressions>
          <expression sequence="0">
            <Math>
              <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
                <apply><plus/><ci>x</ci><ci>y</ci></apply>
              </math>
            </Math>
          </expression>
        </expressions>
      </function>
      <inputs>
        <x unit="\hour">1</x>
        <y unit="\minute">30</y>
      </inputs>
    </algorithm>
    <algorithm namespace="UnitTests.Units.AddLiterAndMilliliter">
      <function>
        <expressions>
          <expression sequence="0">
            <Math>
              <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
                <apply><plus/><ci>x</ci><ci>y</ci></apply>
              </math>
            </Math>
          </expression>
        </expressions>
      </function>
      <inputs>
        <x unit="\litre">1</x>
        <y unit="\milli\litre">250</y>
      </inputs>
    </algorithm>
    <algorithm namespace="UnitTests.Units.SubtractGramFromKilogram">
      <function>
        <expressions>
          <expression sequence="0">
            <Math>
              <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
                <apply><minus/><ci>x</ci><ci>y</ci></apply>
              </math>
            </Math>
          </expression>
        </expressions>
      </function>
      <inputs>
        <x unit="\kilogram">2</x>
        <y unit="\gram">500</y>
      </inputs>
    </algorithm>
    <algorithm namespace="UnitTests.Units.AddLiteralToMeasured">
      <function>
        <expressions>
          <expression sequence="0">
            <Math>
              <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
                <apply><plus/><ci>x</ci><cn>2</cn></apply>
              </math>
            </Math>
          </expression>
        </expressions>
      </function>
      <inputs>
        <x unit="\metre">3</x>
      </inputs>
    </algorithm>
